{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not ask about or consider an applicant's criminal record before making a conditional offer, and after an offer may consider only listed convictions within 6, 4 or 1-year lookbacks, after an individualized assessment with a written denial and appeal right.","key_value":"criminal record review only after conditional offer; 6/4/1-year lookbacks by offense degree","coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent, except units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; providers may still consider methamphetamine-manufacture convictions on federally assisted housing premises and lifetime sex offender registration.","penalty":"Monetary penalties up to $1,000 with no prior violation in five years, $5,000 with one, $10,000 with two or more in seven years; director may order compliance measures and payment to the applicant up to $1,000.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not make any oral or written inquiry regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to making a conditional offer.","interaction":"Does not bar independent rights or actions, including under P.L.1945, c.169 (C.10:5-1 et seq.).","confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure and refund","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether criminal history is part of its eligibility criteria and that the applicant may submit evidence of inaccuracies or rehabilitation; the director may order the fee returned if no housing is provided.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent, except units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Director may require that the applicant's rental application fee be returned unless housing is provided to the applicant.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1)   Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history;","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction after successful provider appeal","requirement":"If a court overturns the director's order and finds the housing provider did not violate the act, the provider may evict a former applicant placed in the unit by that order, with at least 45 days' notice.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"A former applicant residing in a rental dwelling unit placed there by a director's order under the act.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Applies only where the tenant was placed by a director's order under the act"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-63","quoted_span":"shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":"Applies notwithstanding the Anti-Eviction Act, P.L.1974, c.49 (C.2A:18-61.1 et seq.).","confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
